# CODEOWNERS — auto-requests a reviewer when matching files change.
# Copy to `.github/CODEOWNERS` (or repo root). Replace @owner with a GitHub username or team.
# Later patterns win over earlier ones. See:
# https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything in the repo
*                       @<owner>

# Examples — make specific areas owned by specific people/teams:
# /src/auth/            @<security-team>
# *.tf                  @<infra-team>

# The governance files themselves should change deliberately — own them explicitly:
/CLAUDE.md              @<owner>
/REPO_RULES.md          @<owner>
/.claude/               @<owner>
/lefthook.yml           @<owner>
/.gitleaks.toml         @<owner>
